      "writtenOn": "2019-10-23T19:46:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will update p64-\u003elength with p64-\u003ereserved.\n\nreserved field is used for passing extra information (mark_data or buffer_tag etc) along with the buffer to driver. Current QCOM video driver needs this fix.\n\n64 bit clients passing reserved fields to video driver but 32 bit clients are not able to pass because copy_in_user() not available for reserved fields in this function.\n\nIf upstream uses reserved fields then video driver functionality will be broken with that kernel upgrade and it will be fixed in video driver.\n\nBut I believe by the time upstream uses this field QCOM video userspace and driver will be modified and will be upstream compliant to not use reserved fields.",
      "parentUuid": "2f1f1d17_a5b96398",
      "revId": "8f33c492a28a9028ebde7dfe9fbb34e16788cdb6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30632187_13c9c6e3",
        "filename": "drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-compat-ioctl32.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 504,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-23T20:18:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a reason these changes to the video driver can\u0027t be made now to avoid using the reserved field?\n\n\u003e by the time upstream uses this field...\n\nThis is the android-mainline branch which gets updates from linux mainline on every RC. So if upstream changes it in 5.4-rc4, this code will be broken in android-mainline a few days later.\n\nSince this *is* upstream, the code needs to be upstream compliant in this way.",
      "parentUuid": "4d454b89_58d17fab",
      "revId": "8f33c492a28a9028ebde7dfe9fbb34e16788cdb6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
